# agentmemory - per-machine configuration.
#
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env      (or run ..\bootstrap.ps1 -Apply)
#
# .env is gitignored; this file is tracked. The provider credential belongs in
# the repo-root ../.env, never here -- that file loads second, so it is the only
# place an OPENAI_API_KEY can win. See README.md for provider and rollback details.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Console profile - whether to deploy the agent007memory companion console
# (the 3111 proxy + 3114 UI) alongside agentmemory. Uncomment ONE profile.
# See docker-compose.console.yml and agentmemory/README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Compose reads COMPOSE_FILE from this file to decide which compose files to
# merge. The separator defaults to ';' on Windows and ':' elsewhere — pinning it
# to ':' keeps a single .env valid on any host.

# With console (default). MCP clients hit 3111; the console UI is on 3114,
# with per-host /_agent/<name> attribution and optional OpenAI billing sync.
COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml

# Without console. Uncomment this and comment out the line above. agentmemory
# still runs and is reachable, but only on the bypass port 3110 — there is no
# console UI, no per-host tagging, and no billing sync. Nothing else changes.
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Embeddings - local, on-device. Turns off BM25-only mode.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MANDATORY and not cosmetic. Embedding-provider auto-detection runs
#   GEMINI -> OPENAI -> VOYAGE -> COHERE -> OPENROUTER
# so because OPENAI_API_KEY and OPENAI_BASE_URL are both set for the LLM,
# detection would otherwise pick the "openai" embedding provider. Against the
# current vLLM endpoint that is not merely a dimension change but a hard failure:
# <your-llm-host> serves one CHAT model and no embedding model, so every embedding
# request would 404. Pin local explicitly.
#
# Model is Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 at 384 dimensions, baked into the image at
# build time. No API key, no network, no cost.
#
# WARNING: embedding dimension is locked at first write. Switching to a 768- or
# 1536-dim provider later makes agentmemory refuse to boot until you re-embed or
# set AGENTMEMORY_DROP_STALE_INDEX=true (which discards the vectors).
EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=local


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM - vLLM 0.15.0 on <your-llm-host>, serving Qwen/Qwen3-8B-AWQ tensor-parallel
# across both A4000s. One model handles every family; there is no cheap/expensive
# split to make any more. AgentMemory speaks the OpenAI wire protocol, so these
# keep their OPENAI_* names. The credential is in the repo-root .env, which loads
# after this file and is therefore the only place it can win.
#
# CONTEXT IS 16,384 TOKENS - four times smaller than the OpenAI deployment this
# replaced. Every bound below is sized against that, not against cost.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Address is network-specific, so it is a placeholder here. The real value is
# VLLM_BASE_URL in the repo-root .env; copy it in, keeping the /v1 suffix.
#
# It is a TAILSCALE address (100.x.y.z), not a LAN one -- see the notes in
# ../.env.example for why the tailnet IP rather than the MagicDNS name. Verify
# it from INSIDE a container, not just from the host; the two take different
# network paths. If a container cannot reach the tailnet on your host, this
# becomes http://host.docker.internal:<local-port>/v1 pointing at a host-side
# forwarder -- see README.md, "Reaching <your-llm-host> over Tailscale".
OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://100.x.y.z:8000/v1
OPENAI_MODEL=qwen3-8b-awq

# MUST stay empty for vLLM. The deployment patch emits the field on any truthy
# value -- `none` is a non-empty string, so it would put reasoning_effort="none"
# on every request. Empty omits the field entirely.
OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=

# Display-only labels for the console's LLM page, read by docker-compose.yml.
# Without these it keeps claiming "OpenAI API" while talking to <your-llm-host>.
LLM_PROVIDER_LABEL=vLLM
LLM_ENDPOINT_LABEL=<your-llm-host> (Qwen3-8B-AWQ)

# Ollama-era credential for <your-llm-host>, kept only for the documented reversal
# on that host (`sudo systemctl stop vllm && sudo systemctl enable --now ollama`,
# config and models preserved). It is NOT used by the current vLLM provider,
# which authenticates with the key in ../.env. Unused while vLLM is serving.
LLM_HOST_BEARER_TOKEN=replace-me-with-the-<your-llm-host>-bearer-token

# Fail a stalled or queued request instead of holding work indefinitely. Warm
# single-request latency measured 0.05s and 8 parallel requests finished in 0.8s,
# so this is headroom for a cold or contended endpoint, not an expected wait.
AGENTMEMORY_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# Modest parallelism stays well below the account RPM and TPM limits.
SUMMARIZE_CHUNK_CONCURRENCY=2

# Summary map/reduce output can exceed 1,024 tokens on dense sessions. Observation
# compression remains independently capped at 512 below.
MAX_TOKENS=2048
AGENTMEMORY_LLM_CONCURRENCY=3
# Durable file-backed iii queue absorbs hook bursts and survives restarts.
AGENTMEMORY_LLM_QUEUE=agentmemory-llm
AGENTMEMORY_LLM_RECOVERY_BATCH_SIZE=10
# Left unset so the provider falls back to OPENAI_MODEL. One model serves every
# family now, so there is no cheap/expensive split to pin -- and a stale cloud
# model name here would 404 every compression call.
#AGENTMEMORY_COMPRESSION_MODEL=
# Output cap for compression only, independent of MAX_TOKENS.
AGENTMEMORY_COMPRESSION_MAX_TOKENS=512

# Keep summary inputs inside the 16,384-token context. 250 was sized for a
# 65,536-token endpoint and would overflow this one: NOTHING truncates an
# individual observation, and AGENTMEMORY_SUMMARY_MAX_OBSERVATIONS caps the
# observation COUNT, not their size. 16,384 minus the 2,048 output reserve leaves
# roughly 14,000 for the prompt. Raise this only against observed
# `[agentmemory] llm_usage` promptTokens, never by guessing.
SUMMARIZE_CHUNK_SIZE=25

# --- hard prompt ceilings (deployment patch) ---------------------------------
# Backstop applied inside the provider to EVERY family, so no prompt can exceed
# the model context no matter which code path built it. A clamp is logged as
# `llm_input_clamped`; frequent hits mean a family-specific bound below is too
# loose. 48000 chars is ~12k tokens: 16,384 context - 2,048 output - system
# prompt - margin.
AGENTMEMORY_LLM_MAX_INPUT_CHARS=48000

# Consolidation's reflect stage sent every fact, lesson, and untruncated crystal
# narrative matching a concept cluster. With the semantic store past 1,400 facts
# that reached ~26.5k tokens and was rejected outright -- and the stage swallowed
# the error, so it looked like "0 new insights" rather than a failure. These cap
# the input by confidence so the strongest material survives.
# The concept list is its own term and, once bounded, was the largest one: a
# cluster carrying ~700 concept names spent ~17.5k of a 25.5k-char prompt just
# naming them, crowding out the facts. It also grows with every new concept node.
AGENTMEMORY_REFLECT_MAX_CONCEPTS=60
AGENTMEMORY_REFLECT_MAX_FACTS=40
AGENTMEMORY_REFLECT_MAX_LESSONS=20
AGENTMEMORY_REFLECT_MAX_CRYSTALS=5
AGENTMEMORY_REFLECT_MAX_NARRATIVE_CHARS=800
AGENTMEMORY_REFLECT_MAX_PROMPT_CHARS=40000

# Imported/recovered sessions can contain thousands of repetitive hook events.
# Preserve the first 50, last 150, and an even chronological sample between
# them so a single summary stays bounded without disabling summarization.
AGENTMEMORY_SUMMARY_MAX_OBSERVATIONS=500

# Do not reject long-running or imported sessions at the package default of 500.
# The compression input and summary input are independently bounded above.
AGENTMEMORY_MAX_OBSERVATIONS_PER_SESSION=0

# Shard graph nodes, edges, and lookup indexes across 64 small iii KV scopes.
# The first patched startup copies and validates legacy graph state before the
# in-memory switch; legacy scopes remain untouched for rollback.
AGENTMEMORY_GRAPH_STORAGE_V2=true

# OpenAI requires internet access. Search still works offline because embeddings
# remain local; queued LLM work resumes when connectivity returns.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Features
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Graph extraction runs once per completed session, only for observations not
# covered by the last successful batch. It never sends more than 10 at a time.
GRAPH_EXTRACTION_ENABLED=true
AGENTMEMORY_AUTO_GRAPH_MIN_NEW_OBSERVATIONS=10
AGENTMEMORY_AUTO_GRAPH_MAX_OBSERVATIONS_PER_RUN=10

# Terra handles validated semantic consolidation at most once per day.
CONSOLIDATION_ENABLED=true
CONSOLIDATION_COOLDOWN_MS=86400000

# Hooks write recalled context into the agent's conversation at SessionStart.
# Needs no LLM - this is purely a behaviour choice.
#
# THIS VALUE IS ONLY HALF THE SETTING. The flag is read independently on both
# sides: here it gates the server endpoint, and again inside each agent's hook
# process. A container env var cannot reach a hook running on the host, so
# setting it only here leaves every agent write-only: capture works, retrieval
# silently never fires, and the symptom is "the agents only ever push, never
# get" with nothing in any log.
#
# The host side is terminal-stack's (bootstrap/ts-agentmemory.ps1), which patches
# the hook gate to default ON and inlines the value into the hook commands it
# generates. Set AGENTMEMORY_INJECT_CONTEXT=false in the agent's environment to
# turn retrieval off deliberately.
AGENTMEMORY_INJECT_CONTEXT=true

# Stop hooks can fire more than once per agent turn. Summarize a session once it
# has useful volume, then only after 25 new observations (or one hour with any
# new observations). Duplicate stop hooks are serialized per session.
AGENTMEMORY_AUTO_SUMMARIZE=true
AGENTMEMORY_AUTO_SUMMARY_MIN_OBSERVATIONS=10
AGENTMEMORY_AUTO_SUMMARY_MIN_NEW_OBSERVATIONS=25
AGENTMEMORY_AUTO_SUMMARY_MAX_AGE_MS=3600000

# Per-observation LLM compression is ON. Free on local hardware, and it makes
# every downstream prompt smaller: summaries and graph batches consume compressed
# observations rather than raw captures, which is real headroom on a 16k context.
# Captures log compress:"llm" (they logged compress:"synthetic" while it was off).
#
# Expect some observations to cost two calls: the runtime retries once when the
# model returns invalid XML, and an 8B model adheres to the format less reliably
# than a frontier model. Input is bounded by AGENTMEMORY_LLM_MAX_INPUT_CHARS.
AGENTMEMORY_AUTO_COMPRESS=true

# --- console (agent007memory) -------------------------------------------------
# Local checkout of https://github.com/martybytes/agent007memory, used ONLY by
# the update-console scripts: as the source of the SHA pin when deploying, and
# as the build context for --local / -Local dev builds. The normal pinned build
# pulls straight from GitHub and does not need this.
#
# docker-compose.console-local.yml has NO default for this -- set it here (or
# pass it on the command line) before using the local overlay. Absolute path,
# forward slashes on any OS.
#CONSOLE_REPO_PATH=/Users/you/Workspace/src/github.com/martybytes/agent007memory
#CONSOLE_REPO_PATH=C:/DATA/Workspace/src/github.com/martybytes/agent007memory

# --- upstream agentmemory source (optional) -----------------------------------
# Local checkout of https://github.com/rohitg00/agentmemory. Reference material
# only -- NEVER a runtime. The stack builds from npm at AGENTMEMORY_VERSION and
# nothing loads from this path.
#
# It earns its place when patch-agentmemory.mjs fails the build with "package
# layout changed; no match": that patcher applies ~43 exact string replacements
# against the published dist/*.mjs, and this checkout is the readable source
# behind those bundles. It is also the authority for which env var names the
# runtime actually reads.
#
# It MUST sit at the same version this repo pins, or it will confidently answer
# patch questions with the wrong code shape -- worse than having no checkout.
# bootstrap warns when the two disagree. Bumping the pin is a two-step:
#   git -C <path> fetch --tags && git -C <path> checkout v<new-version>
#
# Convention: upstream sources live under Workspace/public/github.com/<repo>;
# your own repos live under Workspace/src/github.com/<org>/<repo>.
#AGENTMEMORY_SOURCE_PATH=/Users/you/Workspace/public/github.com/agentmemory
#AGENTMEMORY_SOURCE_PATH=C:/DATA/Workspace/public/github.com/agentmemory
